.TH MCTX 1 "2026-08-08" "mctx 2.1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mctx \- lightweight terminal notepad for .mctx memory context files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mctx
[\fIfile.mctx\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mctx
is a two-panel terminal editor for the \fI.mctx\fR memory context format used
by AI agents as persistent memory. The left panel lists the sections declared
in the file's \fB%%INDEX\fR block (name, durability tier, version). The right
panel edits the selected section's body. Saving a section bumps its \fIv:\fR
version and rebuilds the byte-offset index.
.PP
If \fIfile.mctx\fR does not exist it is created with a fresh header. If no
file is given, \fImemory.mctx\fR in the current directory is used.
.SH TIERS
Every section carries one durability tier:
.TP
.B !fixed
identity-level facts, never auto-overwritten
.TP
.B !durable
current-state facts, updated in place when superseded
.TP
.B !volatile
short-lived state (checkpoints, scratch), safe to drop
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Tab
switch between the section list and the editor
.TP
.B a
add a new section (prompts for name, then tier)
.TP
.B c
open the \fIcheckpoint\fR section, creating it if missing
.TP
.B Enter
edit the selected section / insert newline in the editor
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
save the current section body (bumps its version)
.TP
.B Esc
back to the section list
.TP
.B q
quit (ignored while the buffer is unsaved); \fBQ\fR quits regardless
.SH FILES
.TP
.I memory.mctx
default memory file
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on normal exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
The \fI.mctx\fR format spec and agent operating guide are distributed with the
project source.
